<p>As a habitual early adopter, I couldn't help but <a href="https://baty.net/posts/2026/10/littlefedi/">install my own instance</a> of <a href="https://littlefedi.org/">littleFedi</a> and kick the tires. It didn't take long before I decided to move there.</p>
<!-- more -->
<p>I liked the software immediately. It was fast, simple (considering all the features), and easy to install.</p>
<p>I put up a poll on Mastodon asking if I should just go for it and migrate to littleFedi or should I post something on Mastodon pointing to the new handle. Within just a few minutes I had enough votes (13 to 0) in favor of fully migrating that I went for it.</p>
<p>An hour later and I'm now <a href="https://social.baty.net/@jack">@jack@social.baty.net</a>.</p>
<p>The nice part is that I'm in complete control of the software that my Fediverse identity runs on. The scary part is the same as the nice part.</p>
